  ('critical-thinking','q3',2,'It presents two options when many others exist, such as past papers, teachers and study groups.'),
  ('critical-thinking','q4',3,'This is a post hoc risk. Another factor is present, so cause has not been shown.'),
  ('critical-thinking','q5',0,'Only the first has a conclusion that must follow if the premises are true. The others do not guarantee their conclusions.'),
  ('critical-thinking','q6',1,'Five answers is a very small sample, so the conclusion is a hasty generalisation.'),
  ('critical-thinking','q7',2,'He notices and remembers evidence that supports his existing belief and ignores the rest.'),
  ('critical-thinking','q8',3,'The first number set your idea of the value, which is anchoring.'),
  ('critical-thinking','q9',0,'Unsourced, urgent messages need checking. Neither sharing nor assuming the opposite is a real check.'),
  ('critical-thinking','q10',1,'The body in charge of the exam, speaking officially, is the most accountable and direct source.'),
  ('critical-thinking','q11',2,'The fair version is the one supporters would accept as their reason. The others are insults or exaggerations.'),
  ('critical-thinking','q12',3,'It claims a small step must lead to disaster without evidence for each step.'),
